# Everything the image must never carry, and everything that would bust the
# build cache without changing the build.
#
# Docker allows one ignore file per build context, and both images here build
# from the repo root: apps/api/Dockerfile and mediacion-app/Dockerfile. So
# nothing either of them needs can be listed. `mediacion-app` used to be
# excluded for the API's benefit; it is required by the web image, and the cost
# is only a larger API build context, never a larger API image — the app is
# never COPYed into the API runtime stage.
#
# Keeping **/dist here matters for both: a local build artifact must never leak
# into an image and get served or executed instead of a freshly built one.
#
# **/*.tsbuildinfo has to go with it. Excluding dist but not the buildinfo that
# describes it is worse than excluding neither: `tsc -b` reads the buildinfo,
# concludes "up to date because newest input src/index.ts is older than output
# tsconfig.tsbuildinfo", and emits nothing — so packages/shared/dist never
# exists and the API build dies on `TS2307: Cannot find module
# '@mediacion/shared'`. It is gitignored, so a fresh clone (what Coolify builds
# from) never had it; only local `docker build` runs after a local `pnpm build`
# hit this, which is exactly the kind of divergence this file exists to prevent.
node_modules
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/.expo
**/coverage
.git
.github
.claude
.vercel
supabase
docs
agents
**/*.log
**/.DS_Store
.env
.env.*
!env.example
